	"department": "CLASS",
	"description": [
		"This course introduces students to the history and art of ancient Greece, from the Bronze Age through the archaic, classical and Hellenistic periods. Students visit every major region of Greece, with extended stays in Athens, Heraklion, and Thessaloniki. When not visiting museums and archaeological sites and learning about ancient Greek civilization, students experience modern Greek culture. Offered annually during Interim."
